content.text:
The user asks two more things:
1. "Add back taste results with the chance of accurate out of 100%" — I think they mean "backtest results with the chance of accuracy out of 100%". So add a backtest results panel: run a historical backtest of the signal strategy on the selected pair (or the universe) and show accuracy % out of 100, plus stats (trades, win rate, profit factor, avg R, max drawdown). "Backtest results with the chance of accurate out of 100%".

2. "Add auto page refresh count down 10seconds" — auto page refresh countdown of 10 seconds. They may want the page/data to refresh every 10 seconds with a visible countdown. Or literally reload the page every 10s. Reloading the whole page every 10s would reset TradingView chart and be awful. Better: auto-refresh market data every 10 seconds with a countdown "10s" indicator, not a full page reload. But they said "auto page refresh count down 10seconds" — likely they want the page to auto-refresh every 10s. I can implement a "Refresh in 10s" countdown that re-runs the scan/data refresh every 10 seconds without reloading the page (preserving login/chart). Explain that it refreshes live data rather than a hard reload to avoid resetting the chart.

However, scanning 24 pairs every 10s is heavy (24 kline requests each time). Maybe auto-refresh only the selected pair data + market tickers every 10s, and full scan every 5m. But user asked auto page refresh 10s. I could implement a 10s "data refresh" that updates:
- ticker prices (one request /ticker/24hr or /ticker/price)
- selected pair klines (1 request)
- live tape
